"https://api.github.com/users/crisbeto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?\n\ncompiler, core\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\nYes\n\n### Description\n\nWe have components that render content in an `ngFor` based on a structure such as\r\n\r\n```\r\ntype ContentAndAdditionalData = {\r\n    content: string;\r\n} & {\r\n    // Can be anything that somewhere has the correct value to track\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhere the items as well as the tracking function is passed through inputs.\r\n\r\nThis has been used like below with the old `ngFor` syntax\r\n\r\n```\r\n@Input() items: Array<...>;\r\n@Input() trackByFn: () => number; \r\n---\r\n*ngFor=\"let item of items; trackBy: trackByFn\" \r\n```\r\n\r\nWith the new `@for` syntax, passing of a tracking function as an input is no longer possible as it yields the error \r\n`ERROR Error: trackByFn is not a function` when done like\r\n\r\n```\r\n<div>\r\n  @for(item of items; track trackByFn($index, item)) {\r\n    <span>{{ item.id }}</span>\r\n  }\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis can be worked around by just tracking by reference as `@for (item of items; track item)` but I would still expect that passing a tracking function as an input should work, or is it no longer possible?\r\n\r\n\n\n### Please provide a link to a minimal reproduction of the bug\n\nhttps://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-uoqxab?file=src%2Fcontrol-flow-with-input%2Fcontrol-flow-with-input.component.html\n\n### Please provide the exception or error you saw\n\n```true\nERROR Error: trackByFn is not a function\n```\n\n\n### Please provide the environment you discovered this bug in (run `ng version`)\n\n```true\n_                      _                 ____ _     ___\r\n    / \\   _ __   __ _ _   _| | __ _ _ __     / ___| |   |_ _|\r\n   / △ \\ | '_ \\ / _` | | | | |/ _` | '__|   | |   | |    | |\r\n  / ___ \\| | | | (_| | |_| | | (_| | |      | |___| |___ | |\r\n /_/   \\_\\_| |_|\\__, |\\__,_|_|\\__,_|_|       \\____|_____|___|\r\n                |___/\r\n    \r\n\r\nAngular CLI: 17.0.7\r\nNode: 18.13.0\r\nPackage Manager: yarn 1.22.19\r\nOS: darwin arm64\r\n\r\nAngular: 17.0.7\r\n... animations, cli, common, compiler, compiler-cli, core, forms\r\n... language-service, platform-browser, platform-browser-dynamic\r\n... router\r\n\r\nPackage                         Version\r\n---------------------------------------------------------\r\n@angular-devkit/architect       0.1700.7\r\n@angular-devkit/build-angular   17.0.7\r\n@angular-devkit/core            17.0.7\r\n@angular-devkit/schematics      17.0.7\r\n@schematics/angular             17.0.7\r\nrxjs                            7.8.1\r\ntypescript                      5.2.2\r\nzone.js                         0.14.2\n```\n\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"dylhunn","id":7135246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMzUyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7135246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn","html_url":"https://github.com/dylhunn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"publ